{"author":{"id":"5698b6d16d951325374257d86a2e673da0e55970c3d21c0f7c6f49018f24e5bf"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1786942197,"nonce":"CL0HzeZXN4NMTiC8RyBR4aAfsXU=","title":"**What is wrong.** `TokenDialog` in `web/src/features/settings/SourcesSection.tsx:752-756` tells the operator, at the one moment they are looking at a secret they can never see again: \"Only a hash is stored, so it cannot be shown again — rotate the source to get a new one.\" Nothing in the UI rotates a source. `POST /api/v1/sources/{id}/rotate-token` exists and is implemented (`api/openapi/openapi.yaml:2425-2464`, `internal/sources/api/sources.go:355-395`), `SourceRow` (`SourcesSection.tsx:277-398`) renders a Test button and a push-enabled checkbox and nothing else, and `web/src/api/endpoints.ts:455-478` wraps `listSources`, `getSource`, `createSource`, `updateSource`, `deleteSource` and `testSource` — not `rotateSourceIngestToken`. The dialog names a recovery path the product does not have.","message":"**The demonstration.** Register a source, close the token dialog without copying the token — the button reads \"I have copied it\" (`SourcesSection.tsx:785`) and closing is the only way out. The token is now unrecoverable by design, the dialog has just said what to do about it, and there is no control anywhere in the app that does it. The remaining path is `curl -X POST .../sources/{id}/rotate-token` with a PAT, which is the credential the sibling ticket says cannot be minted from the UI either.\n\n**Why it matters.** This is the credential a leak actually threatens: an ingest token sits in an Alertmanager config file, often in a git repository or a Helm values file, and rotating it is the whole response to that file being exposed. The handler already carries the operational care the act needs — `internal/sources/api/sources.go:357-361` documents that the old token is rejected with `401` immediately, that Alertmanager treats a `401` as permanent, and that notifications sent between rotation and reconfiguration are lost — and none of that reaches an operator, because the only surface that could tell them is the one that does not exist. The contract makes the same point about retries (`api/openapi/openapi.yaml:2436-2439`): a repeated `Idempotency-Key` is a `409` that rotates nothing, because a blind retry would revoke a secret the caller may still be holding.\n\n**Where.** `web/src/features/settings/SourcesSection.tsx:752-756` (the sentence that promises it), `:277-398` (`SourceRow`, where the control belongs), `:740-790` (`TokenDialog`, which already renders a one-time secret and can be reused verbatim for the rotated one); `web/src/api/endpoints.ts:455-478` (no wrapper); `api/openapi/openapi.yaml:2425-2464`; `internal/sources/api/sources.go:355-395`, which answers the same `SourceCreatedDTO` as create, so the response needs no new type.\n\n**Scope.** small — one endpoint wrapper, one button, one confirmation, and a dialog that already exists.\n\n**Done when.** A source row can rotate its ingest token; the operator is told before confirming that the old token stops working immediately and that alerts sent before the receiver is updated are lost, in the handler's own terms rather than a softened paraphrase; the new secret is shown through the same once-only dialog as the create path; and `TokenDialog`'s sentence about rotating the source names something the reader can do.","files":null}]}